      "role": "user",
      "content": "yeah i get that it's complicated but it feels like there's a lot of data showing that when benefits go up, the incentive to find any kind of job goes down. like, if the government is basically covering your basics, why would someone take a tough retail or service job? isn't that a pretty clear cause and effect for the decline in participation?",
